lg.l:
great city, of prosperous guard, glorious/famous for its
            joyfulness/intoxication/bustle/this joyful, glorious, prosperous, [well]-guarded and
            great city;

the eye of the assembled/united instruments which are the delight of the
            Koel bird (i.e.flute, yāḻ, and drums - UVS - has to be drum here because of the ref to
            the eye) having fallen asleep;

the tongues of pigeons who nest in the eaves [of houses], and of birds
            of the ample water, and of birds who live in the groves having been pressed inside
            [their mouths] (i.e. silenced);
